002_event_collector_guard.ts.patch
==================================

Applies to: KanKyouKen/supabase/functions/event-collector/index.ts

What it does
------------
Validates event_type against the study's registered event_schemas row, writes an
audit_log entry whenever an event is rejected OR when a study has no schema
registered at all, and finally populates events.schema_id -- which is NULL on every
row today, so the versioning table is currently decorative.

Both failure modes are audited on purpose. A rejected event is an incident; a study
running with no registered schema is a silent gap, and silence is exactly what made
the original problem invisible.

audit_log shape (from the live schema): { user_id uuid?, action text, target text }.


STEP 1 -- insert after the has_study_access check (currently ends line 38),
          before the `const response = await fetch(.../events` insert.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  // Resolve the study's registered event schema. Absence is a condition worth
  // recording, not a reason to fail: refusing every event because nobody registered
  // a schema would take the study down.
  let schemaId: string | null = null;
  const schemaRes = await fetch(
    `${ctx.supabaseUrl}/rest/v1/event_schemas?study_id=eq.${body.study_id}` +
    `&select=id,version,definition&order=created_at.desc&limit=1`,
    { headers: { "apikey": ctx.serviceKey, "Authorization": `Bearer ${ctx.serviceKey}` } },
  );
  const [schema] = schemaRes.ok ? await schemaRes.json() : [];

  if (!schema) {
    await audit(ctx, "event_schema_missing",
      `study:${body.study_id}:event_type:${body.event_type}`);
  } else {
    schemaId = schema.id;
    const allowed: string[] = schema.definition?.event_types ?? [];
    if (allowed.length > 0 && !allowed.includes(body.event_type)) {
      await audit(ctx, "event_type_rejected",
        `study:${body.study_id}:participant:${body.participant_id}` +
        `:event_type:${body.event_type}:schema:${schema.version}`);
      throw Errors.badRequest(
        `Unknown event_type "${body.event_type}" for this study (schema ${schema.version})`,
      );
    }
  }


